WEBVTT

00:15.480 --> 00:16.648
Hey, Minato.

00:21.361 --> 00:23.405
Koyun, do- do you like her?

00:30.912 --> 00:32.039
I'd see her around.

00:33.206 --> 00:36.418
And she stood out to me, cause she seemed
different from the other girls at our

00:36.501 --> 00:37.335
school.

00:37.878 --> 00:39.212
So her face stuck with me.

00:40.505 --> 00:41.339
And then…

00:43.759 --> 00:44.593
Huh?

00:47.054 --> 00:48.013
She's alone again.

00:49.431 --> 00:52.100
I was always curious about her whenever
I saw her…

00:52.184 --> 00:53.643
Ever since.

00:55.103 --> 00:57.773
I guess you could say I feel sorry
for her.

01:00.025 --> 01:00.859
Minato.

01:02.235 --> 01:04.780
You always do this to people.

01:04.863 --> 01:07.532
You're always pointing out those who
are on their own and feeling sorry for

01:07.616 --> 01:11.286
them.
But that- that's just so arrogant of you.

01:11.995 --> 01:12.913
I'm arrogant?

01:14.372 --> 01:15.415
You really are.

01:17.000 --> 01:19.503
You feel sorry for people without even
knowing them.

01:19.586 --> 01:22.881
Do you realize how they'd feel
to learn you were only nice to them

01:22.964 --> 01:23.799
out of pity?

01:24.508 --> 01:25.759
You have this savior complex.

01:25.842 --> 01:27.344
You want them to rely on you.

01:27.844 --> 01:29.930
So, in the end, it makes you feel needed.

01:30.639 --> 01:33.141
Koyun does not deserve to be one of your
projects!

03:01.605 --> 03:03.940
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

03:07.736 --> 03:11.740
EPISODE 4
IMPENETRABLE

03:12.782 --> 03:16.536
Minato, you shouldn't look at her as just
another sad soul for you to pity.

03:17.412 --> 03:21.124
She's a person, not a charity case so you
can feel good about yourself.

03:22.667 --> 03:24.544
You know, I think you've got a point.

03:25.503 --> 03:27.005
But I don't feel that way now.

03:27.797 --> 03:31.301
When I first saw her, I did feel
bad for her because she always seemed

03:31.384 --> 03:32.385
to be alone.

03:33.428 --> 03:35.055
But that's clearly changed.

03:36.431 --> 03:37.265
Now…

03:39.643 --> 03:41.228
I'm interested for other reasons.

03:41.311 --> 03:42.270
So don't worry.

03:42.354 --> 03:43.355
Huh?

03:43.438 --> 03:46.566
Well, um, I don't think guys like you are
exactly her type.

03:47.067 --> 03:48.193
That's not what I meant.

03:48.276 --> 03:51.488
And even if I did mean it that way,
at least sugarcoat it. Jeez!

03:51.571 --> 03:52.739
Whatever!

03:53.281 --> 03:55.533
Don't try to put the moves on her
or be weird!

03:55.617 --> 03:56.493
Hey, I mean…

03:56.576 --> 03:58.453
No harm in talking to her.

03:59.287 --> 04:01.206
What're you, like her prison warden?

04:02.415 --> 04:04.501
Helicopter parenting is bad for children.

04:06.211 --> 04:07.254
I just don't want…

04:08.088 --> 04:10.632
I just don't want to hurt Koyun anymore.

04:11.299 --> 04:14.010
Don't you mean you don't want her to get
hurt anymore?

04:14.094 --> 04:16.221
Uh… Hold on.

04:16.304 --> 04:19.891
Is Hikawa the girl from the basketball
team?

04:21.351 --> 04:22.185
Ha! I knew it.

04:22.811 --> 04:25.397
Well, now I can see why you're
so protective.

04:25.480 --> 04:26.481
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

04:31.069 --> 04:34.864
See? This is why I didn't want Koyun
and Minato getting to know each other!

04:34.948 --> 04:37.742
Wait, why is it okay for Yota but not me?

04:38.326 --> 04:40.996
Because you have these crazy, fine-tuned
instincts.

04:41.079 --> 04:43.081
You're saying Yota isn't perceptive?

04:43.164 --> 04:44.040
Well, no, I…

04:44.124 --> 04:45.250
That's pretty rude, y'know.

04:45.333 --> 04:46.167
I meant…

04:49.587 --> 04:50.505
Oh, wow.

04:50.588 --> 04:51.423
Impressive.

04:51.506 --> 04:53.925
The size of your hand is like a sumo
wrestler's.

04:54.884 --> 04:56.970
- Yo!
- Is that a compliment, or…

04:57.053 --> 04:58.263
You're so lucky.

04:58.346 --> 04:59.180
Am I?

04:59.973 --> 05:03.935
When I played basketball, I always
wanted to palm it like this.

05:04.019 --> 05:04.936
Oops.

05:05.020 --> 05:06.646
But I could never pull it off.

05:06.730 --> 05:08.857
That would be pretty hard on your hands.

05:11.484 --> 05:13.278
Wait, hold on. You were…

05:13.361 --> 05:14.529
You played basketball?

05:15.030 --> 05:16.573
Why didn't you say anything?

05:17.073 --> 05:20.118
Oh, cause I wasn't nearly as committed
to it as you were.

05:20.910 --> 05:22.454
And I quit halfway through.

05:24.831 --> 05:25.665
Wait…

05:33.840 --> 05:36.259
The shame from learning someone was
pitying you…

05:37.552 --> 05:38.386
Is that…

05:39.054 --> 05:40.138
Is that how you felt?

05:40.638 --> 05:42.807
Since I first came up and talked to you?

05:42.891 --> 05:43.933
Uh!

05:44.017 --> 05:45.060
Well, I…

05:45.143 --> 05:47.604
- Flustered, flustered!
- You know, I don't really…

05:48.438 --> 05:49.272
I'm sorry.

05:49.939 --> 05:51.566
That really wasn't my intention.

05:54.861 --> 05:57.280
S CRAM SCHOOL INCREASE YOUR CHANCES FOR
PASSING!

06:00.158 --> 06:03.119
- I first talked to you because you
- RIGHT BEFORE THE EXAM! MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

06:03.203 --> 06:06.498
- looked bored all by yourself.
- HIGHEST ACCEPTANCE RATE IN HISTORY

06:06.581 --> 06:07.415
But…

06:07.499 --> 06:10.251
Once I got to know you, I never saw
you that way again.

06:10.794 --> 06:15.840
Since you and I became friends, and then
Yota joined us, I've had so much fun.

06:17.175 --> 06:19.844
I didn't realize you felt all this doubt
and shame.

06:21.429 --> 06:23.139
I'm sorry for making you feel bad.

06:26.643 --> 06:27.477
Minato.

06:30.397 --> 06:32.524
- Whoa.
- Back it up, buddy. You're too close!

06:32.607 --> 06:35.777
Back it up!
I've had a lot of fun with you too.

06:36.653 --> 06:38.238
And you've helped me out a lot!

06:39.489 --> 06:40.323
Jeez!

06:40.407 --> 06:43.159
So, let's keep being friends, okay?

06:47.497 --> 06:48.331
RUB RUB

06:48.415 --> 06:49.999
Your sweater's gonna get dirty.

06:51.334 --> 06:53.545
It wasn't really all that clean to begin
with.

06:53.628 --> 06:54.462
Yeah. Good idea.

06:55.338 --> 06:56.172
Huh?

06:58.341 --> 07:00.093
I guess maybe…

07:01.094 --> 07:04.347
In the end, what I really wanted
was to feel like I was equal in this

07:04.431 --> 07:07.684
friendship, and not just someone he
felt sorry for.

07:10.228 --> 07:12.814
Ugh, I'm such a baby!

07:15.066 --> 07:15.900
Miki?

07:17.193 --> 07:19.320
Yeah, yeah, hold your horses!

07:20.613 --> 07:23.241
Those two just went to buy drinks, right?

07:23.992 --> 07:25.493
Why is it taking them so long?

07:25.577 --> 07:26.411
SLUMP

07:26.494 --> 07:28.455
- They're growing all the cacao
- FOR COCOA

07:28.538 --> 07:30.331
- beans first?
- From scratch?

07:31.249 --> 07:32.917
- Oh.
- Oh.

07:33.001 --> 07:34.711
Sorry for the wait, we're back!

07:34.794 --> 07:36.129
Look, a new flavor.

07:36.212 --> 07:37.464
DOUBLE EXTRA AZUKI BEAN SOUP-RICH

07:37.547 --> 07:38.756
Double Extra Azuki Bean Soup - Rich.

07:38.840 --> 07:40.842
FULL OF BEAN TEXTURE RICH WITH
AZUKI BEANS' SWEETNESS

07:40.925 --> 07:43.386
- We all have to try!
- She said we have no choice.

07:44.345 --> 07:46.055
- Mm?
- Mm?

07:49.142 --> 07:51.561
Not what I expected, but it should
keep us awake.

07:51.644 --> 07:52.812
That's right!

07:52.896 --> 07:55.482
It should at least help us power through
our exams.

07:56.024 --> 07:58.443
Why does Miki look like she's
been crying?

08:02.739 --> 08:04.991
Should I… maybe ask her?

08:07.285 --> 08:08.119
Miki.

08:09.412 --> 08:13.333
Did something happen with Amamiya
when you guys went to buy drinks?

08:14.042 --> 08:15.251
Huh? Oh, we…

08:15.335 --> 08:17.462
- DON'T GET CLOSE TO KOYUN FOR REASONS LIKE
- I mean, um…

08:17.545 --> 08:18.379
THAT

08:18.463 --> 08:19.297
We just chatted.

08:19.380 --> 08:22.467
He did tell me about the time you
bought a curry drink, though.

08:22.550 --> 08:23.551
Why?

08:24.177 --> 08:27.430
He said that he made you buy it
accidentally, so he paid for all of

08:27.514 --> 08:28.348
our drinks today.

08:28.431 --> 08:30.016
THOUGH HE DIDN'T SAY IT HIMSELF

08:30.099 --> 08:31.392
What? He really didn't need to.

08:31.476 --> 08:34.479
See? He didn't tell you cause he
knew you'd feel bad about it.

08:34.562 --> 08:37.690
- 1, X, 2, SOCIETY, W, HAN DYNASTY, ICE,
- Oh, wait. I'm forgetting what we just

08:37.774 --> 08:38.733
- ROME, H2O
- studied!

08:38.816 --> 08:40.360
I need to review! Where's my notebook?

08:40.443 --> 08:42.320
Ugh, c'mon, come back, come back!

08:43.863 --> 08:47.784
If that's all, it still doesn't
explain what might've made her cry.

08:51.829 --> 08:54.249
Time to finally put all that studying and
cramming behind us.

08:54.332 --> 08:57.126
FIRST PERIOD: ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES THIRD

08:57.210 --> 08:59.420
PERIOD: BASIC CHEMISTRY, SHR NUMBER OF
STUDENTS: 30

08:59.504 --> 09:00.463
First day of exams.

09:01.464 --> 09:02.423
And begin.

09:07.011 --> 09:07.845
Hm?

09:08.596 --> 09:10.014
It's exactly the same.

09:10.098 --> 09:11.683
Thank you, past exams.

09:13.768 --> 09:16.145
We've been over this problem already with
Yota!

09:24.821 --> 09:26.114
Off to a good start!

09:26.197 --> 09:27.031
Yay!

09:29.492 --> 09:30.994
FIRST PERIOD: LANGUAGE CULTURE 9:00-9:50

09:31.077 --> 09:31.911
SECOND PERIOD: LOGIC AND EXPRESSION AND

09:31.995 --> 09:32.829
I've got this. I've actually got this!

09:32.912 --> 09:34.872
EXPRESSION 10:00-10:50

09:40.545 --> 09:42.797
THIRD PERIOD: GEOGRAPHY 11:00-11:50

09:42.880 --> 09:44.591
- FOURTH PERIOD: BIOLOGY 12:00-12:50
- Alright.

09:44.674 --> 09:45.508
Your time's up.

10:04.402 --> 10:05.486
Notifications?

10:06.195 --> 10:08.781
- NINE MIKI: 9 NOTIFICATIONS
- And quite a few of them.

10:08.865 --> 10:09.949
Koyun.

10:10.033 --> 10:12.243
Let's grab lunch somewhere on
the way home.

10:12.327 --> 10:13.494
Oops, group chat.

10:13.578 --> 10:14.537
Wanna join Yota?

10:14.621 --> 10:16.623
You're not an afterthought, I swear!

10:16.706 --> 10:17.540
Please come.

10:18.082 --> 10:19.667
Sure, I'll come.

10:19.751 --> 10:21.002
Koyun, come on!

10:22.545 --> 10:24.047
Oh, there you are, Koyun.

10:26.883 --> 10:29.469
Looks like you and I are the first ones
to meet up.

10:30.094 --> 10:31.888
Miki's still in the classroom?

10:34.932 --> 10:36.017
What's going on?

10:36.976 --> 10:37.852
What's wrong, Miki?

10:37.935 --> 10:40.104
Oh, Minato. Yota…?

10:40.188 --> 10:41.314
He went downstairs.

10:41.397 --> 10:43.358
Wait, did he leave already?

10:43.441 --> 10:44.651
Need something from him?

10:45.318 --> 10:48.946
It's just Koyun, Yota, and I, we made
lunch plans.

10:51.407 --> 10:53.868
- What gives, Miki?
- Ah! It's freezing!

10:53.951 --> 10:56.621
Are you trying to leave me out of
your good time?

10:56.704 --> 10:58.665
N- N- No that's, uh, not it at all!

10:58.748 --> 11:00.500
BUOONO BUONO!!

11:01.417 --> 11:02.251
Stare.

11:03.711 --> 11:06.255
What?
Five more? I can't tell what's different.

11:06.756 --> 11:07.965
The grapes maybe?

11:08.049 --> 11:09.133
It isn't.

11:09.217 --> 11:10.677
I found a difference.

11:10.760 --> 11:12.220
- BUOONO BUONO!! MENU
- And another one.

11:12.303 --> 11:14.514
- Oh.
- Jeez, you're too fast. Hold up.

11:15.098 --> 11:18.059
If we don't find all of 'em soon,
our food's not gonna come.

11:18.142 --> 11:19.560
Is that really how it works?

11:21.312 --> 11:24.273
They're just acting like regular friends.

11:25.024 --> 11:25.858
I'm glad.

11:27.276 --> 11:30.363
SPACING OUT

11:30.446 --> 11:32.115
Am I reading too much into it?

11:32.198 --> 11:34.033
Have you been here before, Hikawa?

11:34.117 --> 11:34.951
Hm?

11:35.451 --> 11:36.494
Not really.

11:36.577 --> 11:37.412
First time.

11:38.246 --> 11:40.790
I don't normally go anywhere after
school.

11:42.500 --> 11:43.626
Uh. Whoa.

11:45.044 --> 11:47.338
Is that pity I see creeping into
your eyes?

11:47.839 --> 11:48.840
Is it?

11:49.632 --> 11:50.717
That's not it.

11:51.426 --> 11:53.136
- CAFÉ RESTAURANT BUOONO BUONO!!
- Bon appetit!

11:53.219 --> 11:54.345
- Bon appetit!
- Bon appetit!

11:54.429 --> 11:56.347
It was cheap but actually pretty good.

12:00.643 --> 12:01.686
So, Hikawa…

12:02.270 --> 12:03.855
You're not in any clubs, right?

12:04.439 --> 12:05.565
Do you work part-time?

12:06.274 --> 12:07.233
Uh, yeah.

12:07.734 --> 12:10.069
But honestly, I don't work that
many shifts.

12:10.153 --> 12:11.195
Where do you work?

12:11.696 --> 12:13.656
REGULAR CUSTOMERS

12:13.740 --> 12:16.701
A laid-back spot only the elderly in the
neighborhood come to.

12:16.784 --> 12:20.455
- It's just a local restaurant.
- So then what do you do in your free time?

12:20.538 --> 12:22.665
- Give it a rest, would you?
- Good question.

12:22.749 --> 12:24.000
How do I spend my time?

12:25.543 --> 12:26.544
I read books.

12:30.131 --> 12:32.175
What is this? It looks boring.

12:32.884 --> 12:34.093
I watch movies.

12:34.635 --> 12:36.304
Is this even interesting?

12:37.013 --> 12:38.306
And I study ahead.

12:38.806 --> 12:40.099
You're such a nerd.

12:42.310 --> 12:43.436
Nothing, really.

12:44.771 --> 12:46.689
Just space out most of the time.

12:47.899 --> 12:48.733
Oh, really?

12:49.275 --> 12:50.443
That's kind of a shame.

12:50.985 --> 12:51.819
Glare!

12:52.403 --> 12:54.781
Koyun spends her free time hanging out
with me!

12:54.864 --> 12:55.990
Does she really?

13:01.621 --> 13:03.039
Are you paying separately?

13:03.122 --> 13:03.998
Yes.

13:04.499 --> 13:06.417
- Hey. Minato, what are you doing?
- Mm?

13:07.001 --> 13:08.336
What's with the interrogation?

13:08.419 --> 13:09.545
I told you, didn't I?

13:10.129 --> 13:11.672
Well, I figured…

13:12.715 --> 13:15.384
If we were the only ones involved in
the conversation, she'd be bored.

13:15.468 --> 13:17.136
- SLICK, SLICK
- Oh!

13:17.220 --> 13:18.888
- You have a point!
- Right?

13:22.809 --> 13:26.145
All of these questions are kind of
exhausting.

13:29.023 --> 13:31.442
- Whew, man, I am crazy full.
- The people and environment are so

13:31.526 --> 13:32.735
different from back then.

13:32.819 --> 13:34.195
I'm going to burst.

13:34.862 --> 13:37.657
I'm still not very good at talking about
myself.

13:39.283 --> 13:40.868
I don't hate him or anything.

13:41.452 --> 13:44.455
But I'm scared of people finding out
who I am on the inside.

13:45.206 --> 13:47.083
I'm trying to avoid rejection.

13:47.792 --> 13:50.753
To avoid hating myself more than I
already do.

13:52.213 --> 13:55.508
That's why I keep my distance when
people try to get close to me.

13:55.591 --> 13:57.051
God, you're such a weirdo.

13:57.134 --> 13:57.969
You know that?

14:00.137 --> 14:01.472
What is normal anyway?

14:05.476 --> 14:06.477
SECOND TRIMESTER FINAL EXAMS DAY 3

14:06.561 --> 14:07.395
FIRST PERIOD: MODERN JAPANESE 09:00-09:50

14:07.478 --> 14:08.312
Good job! We nailed those exams!

14:08.396 --> 14:10.648
SECOND PERIOD: BASIC BIOLOGY 10:00-10:50

14:10.731 --> 14:11.774
EXAM AFTER-PARTY CLASS 1-5

14:11.858 --> 14:12.692
- Yay!
- Yay!

14:12.775 --> 14:15.111
- Yay!
- It looks delicious. Do you wanna try it?

14:15.194 --> 14:16.529
Sure, I'll have a bite.

14:16.612 --> 14:17.530
Ahh.

14:18.030 --> 14:20.783
Azumi is absolutely glowing today.

14:25.204 --> 14:26.664
I'm sick to my stomach.

14:27.540 --> 14:30.084
I somehow managed to get through
the exams, but…

14:30.167 --> 14:32.753
My stomach feels so queasy.

14:33.754 --> 14:34.964
SCHOOL NURSE'S OFFICE

14:35.464 --> 14:36.966
- Noriko.
- Huh?

14:37.466 --> 14:38.509
Help.

14:38.593 --> 14:40.553
Are you seriously back here already?

14:41.053 --> 14:43.806
I keep telling you this isn't the place
to get warm.

14:43.890 --> 14:45.933
I'm actually sick today, I swear.

14:47.018 --> 14:47.852
Oh.

14:53.316 --> 14:54.275
It's my stomach.

14:55.359 --> 14:56.903
Oh no. You stressed?

14:56.986 --> 14:58.988
Or did you eat something you shouldn't
have?

14:59.071 --> 15:01.240
I haven't eaten anything today.

15:01.782 --> 15:04.076
Oh, I had three cups of coffee, though.

15:05.244 --> 15:06.287
That'll do it.

15:06.370 --> 15:08.289
Okay, you can sleep it off here.

15:08.998 --> 15:11.542
I can't get comfortable laying in
my uniform.

15:11.626 --> 15:13.294
Alright, don't push it, kid.

15:18.966 --> 15:21.552
Did you go to junior high with anyone
here at Meiten?

15:21.636 --> 15:23.429
I did actually. He was a nerd.

15:24.347 --> 15:26.766
Well, yeah, you have to be smart to
get in here.

15:28.267 --> 15:29.393
What about you, Igarashi?

15:29.477 --> 15:30.311
You know anyone?

15:30.895 --> 15:31.729
Ah?

15:32.897 --> 15:34.315
I have no idea.

15:34.398 --> 15:36.984
No one I know would get in here.

15:38.152 --> 15:40.112
We have some snacks left, I think.

15:40.780 --> 15:41.822
Did we buy too much?

15:41.906 --> 15:43.574
- Yeah, we might have.
- Mm-hm.

15:43.658 --> 15:44.992
Aren't those guys from West High?

15:45.076 --> 15:45.993
Mm.

15:46.077 --> 15:46.911
Huh?

15:48.412 --> 15:49.330
Igarashi?

15:51.082 --> 15:53.250
- What the… What?
- What?

16:00.508 --> 16:03.552
Head on home.
I gotta catch up with someone.

16:04.053 --> 16:05.137
Okay, have fun.

16:06.055 --> 16:06.889
Bye, Miki.

16:07.974 --> 16:08.849
Why are you here?

16:11.435 --> 16:12.269
Azumi.

16:13.229 --> 16:14.063
You…

16:14.563 --> 16:15.439
I what?

16:16.565 --> 16:18.776
You just look so different than you
used to.

16:19.443 --> 16:20.528
Where'd "gorilla" go?

16:21.696 --> 16:23.155
Shut up! Do not call me that!

16:24.031 --> 16:24.865
Mm.

16:27.785 --> 16:28.619
Hm?

16:28.703 --> 16:30.371
Why're you at this school?

16:30.454 --> 16:31.372
Huh?

16:31.455 --> 16:32.915
I'm here for club activities.

16:33.457 --> 16:35.626
We have a joint soccer practice.

16:37.169 --> 16:39.797
By the way, I didn't know you went to
Meiten.

16:40.423 --> 16:44.051
I bet you're probably the only one
who commutes this far every day, huh?

16:44.593 --> 16:45.428
Why bother?

16:46.345 --> 16:48.848
I guess he doesn't know Koyun goes here
too.

16:49.765 --> 16:50.599
Hm?

16:51.183 --> 16:52.727
Hey! Igarashi!

16:52.810 --> 16:53.978
What's the hold up?

16:54.478 --> 16:55.438
Oh.

16:56.188 --> 16:57.064
Oh, sorry.

16:57.606 --> 16:58.649
See ya later.

17:02.319 --> 17:03.404
Who was that girl?

17:03.487 --> 17:04.447
She's so cute.

17:04.530 --> 17:06.115
Dude, get your eyes checked.

17:06.198 --> 17:07.241
Huh?

17:08.117 --> 17:08.951
Koyun.

17:09.035 --> 17:11.704
Please tell me you've already gone
home from school.

17:17.209 --> 17:19.754
So dark. Wait. What time is it?

17:20.921 --> 17:23.340
Oh, it's just because the curtains were
closed.

17:23.424 --> 17:24.925
Thanks, Noriko.

17:26.052 --> 17:29.638
It's still pretty bright outside, so
at least it hasn't been that long.

17:35.895 --> 17:36.729
Igarashi!

17:38.105 --> 17:39.231
Right, that was today!

17:39.982 --> 17:42.943
Well, he's visiting our school soon,
but you don't know each other, so never

17:43.027 --> 17:44.904
- mind.
- When?

17:44.987 --> 17:47.073
For a scrimmage on the last day of exams.

17:48.532 --> 17:49.784
He told me about it, but…

17:50.951 --> 17:51.994
Oh, by the way…

17:52.703 --> 17:54.497
Earlier, I ran into Azumi.

17:54.997 --> 17:56.832
Are you two classmates?

17:56.916 --> 17:58.334
Oh. Miki?

17:58.417 --> 18:00.002
Not classmates, but friends.

18:01.212 --> 18:03.089
So, is she causing trouble here too?

18:03.172 --> 18:04.465
She broken any windows?

18:06.092 --> 18:07.051
Nah, she's great.

18:07.551 --> 18:10.471
Earlier, I ran into Azumi. Are you two
classmates?

18:10.554 --> 18:12.014
They're talking about Miki.

18:12.098 --> 18:13.766
- Oh, Miki?
- Why?

18:13.849 --> 18:15.184
Not classmates, but friends

18:15.267 --> 18:16.519
Agh, I can't hear them very well.

18:16.602 --> 18:17.937
…Causing trouble here too?

18:19.230 --> 18:20.940
Hikawa. What are you doing?

18:22.233 --> 18:23.692
Um, I was just…

18:24.235 --> 18:25.694
Are you feeling any better?

18:25.778 --> 18:26.612
Yeah, I'm fine.

18:27.113 --> 18:29.448
- Can you go home?
- Yes.

18:32.827 --> 18:34.829
I'm gonna book it so he won't notice me.

18:38.249 --> 18:41.794
I couldn't hear everything, but they were
definitely talking about Miki.

18:41.877 --> 18:44.046
They're not gonna talk about me,
are they?

18:47.591 --> 18:51.512
I wonder if Amamiya will bring me up.

18:52.638 --> 18:53.806
You know Igarashi?

18:54.515 --> 18:57.476
Where do you work?
Whadda you do in your spare time?

18:57.560 --> 18:58.936
SO CURIOUS ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE

18:59.019 --> 18:59.854
I bet he will.

19:02.231 --> 19:03.065
I'd hate that.

19:04.692 --> 19:07.027
I don't want people having any
interest in me.

19:12.867 --> 19:16.120
I don't want anyone to know my true self.

19:17.997 --> 19:18.831
Oh.

19:18.914 --> 19:22.209
By the way, Igarashi, do you remember
Hikawa?

19:25.504 --> 19:26.338
Huh?

19:36.891 --> 19:37.933
Oh, Hikawa!

19:40.311 --> 19:41.770
Hey there! Good morning!

19:41.854 --> 19:42.897
Eh?

19:42.980 --> 19:45.149
Why does he look all warm like that?

19:48.777 --> 19:50.613
Oh! We just finished morning practice.

19:50.696 --> 19:52.656
- Amamiya, did you run here, or something?
- I'm steaming from the cold.

19:52.740 --> 19:54.742
Morning practice. Boy, I remember those.

19:56.869 --> 20:00.039
Oh.
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

20:02.333 --> 20:03.167
Although…

20:03.834 --> 20:05.377
You don't really care, do you?

20:06.086 --> 20:09.048
Seems like you weren't close friends
with him, or anything.

20:10.966 --> 20:11.800
Huh?

20:11.884 --> 20:13.219
Where did that come from?

20:14.094 --> 20:17.181
Tell me, was Igarashi super popular
back in junior high?

20:18.307 --> 20:20.392
Well, I mean, I guess so.

20:21.435 --> 20:24.313
He was always the center of attention.

20:24.396 --> 20:27.024
- With people constantly around him.
- I knew it.

20:27.524 --> 20:29.026
Figured he was like that.

20:30.027 --> 20:33.948
He's the kind of person who just butts
his nose into other people's business…

20:34.031 --> 20:35.199
Without even asking.

20:36.158 --> 20:37.952
Oh. I'm sorry.

20:38.452 --> 20:40.704
Let's stop talking about junior high.

20:44.500 --> 20:45.334
Hey, don't worry.

20:45.417 --> 20:47.628
You'll make all new memories in
high school.

20:48.379 --> 20:51.173
There's a lot of events, and fun stuff
coming up.

20:53.092 --> 20:55.886
There's the dance, and field day too.
Oh, and don't forget soccer season.

20:55.970 --> 20:57.721
Speaking of which, any chance you
might come to some of our games?

20:57.805 --> 21:00.224
I've never talked to Amamiya about my
memories from junior high school, so…

21:00.307 --> 21:01.892
Why'd he suddenly mention them?

21:02.810 --> 21:03.936
Did he hear something?

21:04.478 --> 21:05.562
From Igarashi?

21:06.563 --> 21:08.315
What did he tell him?

21:09.275 --> 21:11.193
Koyuki. Oh my gosh, no way!

21:11.277 --> 21:12.778
You're really dating Igarashi?

21:13.279 --> 21:14.196
So…

21:14.280 --> 21:15.614
How far have you two gone?

21:17.283 --> 21:18.117
It's funny.

21:18.200 --> 21:19.660
She only seems to be nice to guys,
am I right?

21:19.743 --> 21:21.370
I know, right? What a "pick-me."

21:22.371 --> 21:23.747
- Did you know?
- Igarashi is…

21:23.831 --> 21:24.832
I heard Koyuki's family is…

21:24.915 --> 21:26.625
- No way.
- You're kidding!

21:27.960 --> 21:28.794
What? Seriously?

21:28.877 --> 21:31.505
- Why does everyone love rumors and
- So that rumor was true.

21:31.588 --> 21:34.466
- Gossip so much?
- Why can't they just leave me alone?

21:34.550 --> 21:36.010
Hey, Koyuki.

21:37.636 --> 21:40.306
Do you get some sick pleasure in
meddling in my life?

21:40.806 --> 21:42.725
What's really going on with you two?

21:43.600 --> 21:45.311
You don't care if it's true or not…

21:45.394 --> 21:47.604
Just as long as it's entertaining, right?

21:52.818 --> 21:53.777
Well, I'm done.

21:56.989 --> 21:58.157
Mind your own business.

21:59.700 --> 22:01.368
- I don't get it.
- Uh?

22:02.619 --> 22:03.454
WARM, WARM

22:03.537 --> 22:05.122
Ah, the cold air feels so good.

22:07.124 --> 22:07.958
Huh?

22:08.042 --> 22:10.377
- Koyu-
- Why do you have to be such a busybody?

22:15.007 --> 22:16.091
I don't understand.

22:19.595 --> 22:20.679
It makes me sick.
